# GitHub checks must pass on a PR

When this message asks to create a pull request, the job is not done at `gh pr create`.

1. Run local `yarn lint`, `yarn format:check`, `yarn type-check`, and `yarn test:ci` first.
2. Commit, push, and open the PR only if this message asked.
3. Wait on GitHub: `gh pr checks --watch` (or poll `gh pr checks`) until every required check has a conclusion.
4. Do not tell the user the PR is done while checks are pending or red.
5. If a check fails: fix it, commit, and push on that same branch. That is part of the PR ask. Then wait again until green.

Local `yarn test:ci` is not GitHub. Do not skip the wait because a file was not touched or because it passed on the laptop.
